2
00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:07.900
[Instructor] Now we have
our "Game Over Text"

3
00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:11.166
for our player and we actually need

4
00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:13.300
to be able to turn it off and on.

5
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.633
So what we'll do is 
on our Game Over Text Element

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.300
in our Hierarchy,
if we disable the GameObject

7
00:00:21.566 --> 00:00:23.833
by clicking on the checkbox
in our Inspector

8
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.866
next to the Game Over Text field,

9
00:00:25.966 --> 00:00:27.800
you can see that now our text

10
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.800
has disappeared from the scene

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.800
which is good, 
that's exactly what we wanted.

12
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.466
Now we'll write some codes
so that we can turn this back on.

13
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:37.033
Now in our GameManager Script,

14
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.633
we'll add another reference
to our Game Over Text,

15
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:42.433
similar to what we did
with our score text.

16
00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:45.533
We'll make it public
so we can assign that reference,

17
00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:53.000
that'll be a "TextMeshProUGUI,"
we'll call it gameOverText,

18
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.233
and then in Start() we're just
going to test and see.

19
00:00:57.866 --> 00:01:04.933
So if we use gameOverText
and then we use the actual gameObject,

20
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:07.333
we'll set that gameObject
back to active.

21
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.566
Now make sure that you use Boolean,
so we use true so that we can set

22
00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.900
our gameObject back to active
since we disabled it.

23
00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:19.766
Then as a quick test we're going
to play our game

24
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:26.300
and we should have seen
the text pop up right here.

25
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.100
Lets see, so it didn't actually set
the reference to our Game Over Text

26
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.266
in our Game Manager,
so I should do that first.

27
00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:38.766
So now lets just see, make sure.

28
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.366
Press play, and then Game Over should
pop up right there, perfect, cool.

29
00:01:45.633 --> 00:01:47.500
So what you're gonna do is

30
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.566
you're going to go to your
Game Over Text in your Hierarchy,

31
00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:53.800
uncheck the checkbox on the top right

32
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.400
at the top of your Inspector
so that way we disable the GameObject.

33
00:01:57.866 --> 00:02:01.833
In your GameManager Script
make sure that you create a variable

34
00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:04.400
for the gameOverText
and make it public so that way

35
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.366
we can set it inside of Unity

36
00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:09.300
and then in your Start() method
just to test it out we're going

37
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.733
to set that gameObject
to be active again

38
00:02:11.733 --> 00:02:15.000
so that way when we play our game,
it should just pop up on the screen.

39
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.433
Now it's your turn.

